# {{NAME}}

A Hugo theme, generated from the scaffold of Hugo {{HUGO_VERSION}}.
Hugo knows it as `{{SLUG}}`.

## Working on it

```sh
./c check                every gate in order, stopping at the first failure
./c serve                the fixture site, with live reload on a template edit
./c conform              build against the scaffold and against this theme, then diff
./c feature list         every feature, installed or available
./c help                 the rest
```

`./c check` passes on the theme as generated. Every change from here is
measured against that.

## What conformance means

A fixture site builds twice. Once against the scaffold of the installed
Hugo, once against this theme.

The file list and the shape of every page are compared. The theme has to
publish the same pages, and put the same headings, links and images on
them.

Markup and styling are free to differ. What a reader can find on the
page is not.

## Before releasing

`theme.toml` needs a description, tags, features and a demo site, and
`images/screenshot.png` and `images/tn.png` have to exist at 1500x1000
and 900x600. `./c check gate=release` lists what is missing.
